            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;geolocation&gt;</code> element; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5125006551416832\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5125006551416832</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds support data for the element itself and the associated <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLGeolocationElement</code> DOM interface.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'll set this to a draft for now, because the specification URL hasn't yet been added to browser-specs. See <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3350035969\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/2107\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/browser-specs/issues/2107/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/2107\">w3c/browser-specs#2107</a> for progress on that.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28801",
            "title": "Chrome 144 geolocation element",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-12T17:54:32.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-12T17:53:50.000Z",
            "author": {
